        "description",
        "substrate",
        "run_length",
        "colours",
        "due_date",
        "quoted_price"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "ai_knowledge": {
    "domain_notes": "Quoting is the risk point: run length changes unit economics non-linearly because make-ready is a fixed cost spread over the run, so short runs priced off long-run rates lose money every time. Waste has to be logged per job or estimates never improve. Signed proof approval is the defence against a reprint dispute.",
    "starter_prompts": [
      "Show job costing against quote for last month.",
      "What is waste percentage by press?",
      "Show press schedule for this week.",
      "Which jobs are awaiting proof approval?"
    ]
  }
}
